<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hawk-Dove mixed ESS" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "When the cost of injury exceeds the value of the contested resource, the stable outcome is a mixture in which animals escalate with probability equal to the ratio of resource value to injury cost." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "payoffs E(H,H) = (V-C)/2, E(H,D) = V, E(D,H) = 0, E(D,D) = V/2; for C > V the unique ESS plays Hawk with probability p^* = V/C" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: symmetric pairwise contests, fixed V and C, no role asymmetries (asymmetries such as ownership give the Bourgeois ESS instead). Formal status: proved within the game." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Experimentally vary resource value and the expected cost of fighting in a contest system, and test that escalation frequency tracks V/C." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "John Maynard Smith (1982) Evolution and the Theory of Games" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/246015a0> .
}
